  "aiContextParagraph": "As Brazil observes Black Friday 2026, consumer attention has turned toward both the potential for significant discounts and the risks of deceptive retail practices. A study conducted by Jusbrasil notes that misleading advertising is the leading subject of court decisions related to the shopping event, which is frequently referred to locally as 'Black Fraude.' Beyond retail consumer goods, the event has expanded into broader markets, with organizations such as Banco do Brasil conducting property auctions featuring properties without minimum bids, and construction firms offering special purchase conditions. Media outlets have provided extensive coverage on consumer safety, including tips to avoid online scams, advice on international currency payments for those shopping in locations like Orlando, and analysis regarding the optimal timing for securing the best discounts. Furthermore, approximately 70 percent of consumers surveyed have expressed concerns about being misled by promotional campaigns.",
